 "requirement": "A fixed hold angle of -4.7 deg reaches 5 N when only the softest finger A deflects (F_target / k_min at the pad).",
 "notes": "gap_tip = a - xf_A - xf_B - pads + finger root float (X, each finger) + servo angle error (both fingers) + finger-B backlash lag. The CAD mesh is centred (README tooth phasing), so when A drives B closed B lags the CAD theta = 0 by jt/(2r), not jt/r. theta = 0 means rigid pads 1 mm apart (DESIGN-BASIS R18). Interference-to-force: the base force variants use 2F/k at the pad (both fingers compliant, equal k). DESIGN-BASIS D7 backs finger B with a rigid FSR plate, so the -rigidB variants use k_B -> infinity: only A deflects and the pad interference for force F is F/k_A. The -pinned variant is the fix-9 layout (T06-bushed / T07-bushed) plus the dog coupling's lash, which rotates both fingers together (tip sensitivity 2 L_tip, like the servo angle error).",
